    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide069Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide069Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Public company</dt><dd>Company with securities available in public markets and reporting obligations defined by its jurisdiction and listing structure.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Treasury strategy</dt><dd>Policy for holding and managing corporate assets, including cash, securities, bitcoin, or other investments.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Corporate bitcoin</dt><dd>Bitcoin owned or controlled by a company or consolidated entity rather than held for a customer.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Customer assets</dt><dd>Assets held or administered for clients under a custody, brokerage, trust, or service arrangement.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Fair value</dt><dd>Measurement based on an asset’s market value under an applicable accounting framework.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Unrealized gain or loss</dt><dd>Change in reported value before an asset is sold or otherwise disposed of.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Capital structure</dt><dd>Mix of common equity, preferred securities, debt, cash, and other claims financing a company.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Dilution</dt><dd>Reduction in an existing shareholder’s proportional ownership when additional shares or share-linked securities are issued.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Custodian</dt><dd>Entity responsible under contract and law for safeguarding assets or the credentials that control them.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Exchange-traded product</dt><dd>Publicly traded security or trust interest designed to provide exposure under a defined legal structure.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Filed disclosure</dt><dd>Information submitted to a regulator; evidence of what the filer represented, not automatic proof of operational effectiveness.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Protocol authority</dt><dd>Claimed power to set Bitcoin consensus rules; corporate ownership, market value, or product reach does not provide unilateral protocol authority.</dd></div></dl></section>
